From c2ab84f62f29418533883e820622e96fa66f74c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Shevchenko <andriy.shevchenko@linux.intel.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Apr 2024 17:26:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 056/934] drm/panel: ili9341: Respect deferred probe

[ Upstream commit 740fc1e0509be3f7e2207e89125b06119ed62943 ]

GPIO controller might not be available when driver is being probed.
There are plenty of reasons why, one of which is deferred probe.

Since GPIOs are optional, return any error code we got to the upper
layer, including deferred probe. With that in mind, use dev_err_probe()
in order to avoid spamming the logs.

