From 7926439f9fafa44281aa879d545e5cbab1e9c894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thadeu Lima de Souza Cascardo <cascardo@igalia.com>
Date: Fri, 24 May 2024 11:47:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 699/934] sock_map: avoid race between sock_map_close and
 sk_psock_put

commit 4b4647add7d3c8530493f7247d11e257ee425bf0 upstream.

sk_psock_get will return NULL if the refcount of psock has gone to 0, which
will happen when the last call of sk_psock_put is done. However,
sk_psock_drop may not have finished yet, so the close callback will still
point to sock_map_close despite psock being NULL.

This can be reproduced with a thread deleting an element from the sock map,
while the second one creates a socket, adds it to the map and closes it.

That will trigger the WARN_ON_ONCE:

