From a556bdd9d635af1352b0a6876e3fad1d3303147a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tony Luck <tony.luck@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Apr 2024 14:19:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 820/934] x86/cpu/vfm: Add new macros to work with
 (vendor/family/model) values

[ Upstream commit e6dfdc2e89a0adedf455814c91b977d6a584cc88 ]

To avoid adding a slew of new macros for each new Intel CPU family
switch over from providing CPU model number #defines to a new
scheme that encodes vendor, family, and model in a single number.

  [ bp: s/casted/cast/g ]

